3. How a Browser Requests and Displays a Web Page
Steps:
User enters a URL in the browser (e.g., www.example.com).


The browser converts it into an HTTP request and sends it to the web server.


The DNS translates the domain name into the server’s IP address.


The server processes the request and sends back an HTML file (and other resources like CSS/JS).


The browser rendering engine parses HTML, applies CSS, runs JS, and displays the webpage visually to the user.



